-- title:
--   From HTo G Avg Over Tail Type Ev
-- statement:
--   **A fixed-type tail average is the expectation of an averaged sandwich total.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `psi_bi` be a quantum state, let `family` be an indexed polynomial family, let `n` be a natural number, let `tau` be a Boolean type pattern of length `n`, and let `B` be any operator on the local index set `ι`. For each point tuple `xs`, let `T` denote the G-hat half-product operator for a tuple `gs`. Then
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb{E}_{xs\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\operatorname{PointTuple}(n))}
--   \sum_{\substack{gs:\,\operatorname{gHatTupleType}(gs)=\tau}}
--   \operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{bi}}\!\left(\operatorname{leftTensor}(TT^{\dagger})\,\operatorname{rightTensor}(B)\right)
--   =
--   \operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{bi}}\!\left(
--   \operatorname{leftTensor}\!\left(\bigl(\operatorname{averagedSandwichByTypeSubMeas}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},n,\tau)\bigr).\operatorname{total}\right)
--   \operatorname{rightTensor}(B)\right).
--   $$
--
--   This folds the uniform tail-point and exact-type outcome average into the stored per-type sandwich submeasurement. It is used in the collapsed `M₄` calculation, the tail-stage recurrence branch, and the self-consistency context bound.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_avgOver_tail_type_ev`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
